ge study with long-term follow-up</article-title><source>Histopathology</source><year>1991</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>403</fpage><lpage>410</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Histopathology||19|403||bib4|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1757079</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib5"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ernster</surname><given-names>VL</given-names></name><name><surname>Barclay</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Increases in ductal carcinoma <italic>in situ</italic> (DCIS) of the breast in relation to mammography: a dilemma</article-title><source>J Natl Cancer Inst Monogr</source><year>1997</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>151</fpage><lpage>156</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Natl Cancer Inst Monogr||22|151||bib5|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9709292</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ernster</surname><given-names>VL</given-names></name><name><surname>Barclay</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kerlikowske</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Grady</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Henderson</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Incidence of and treatment for ductal carcinoma <italic>in situ</italic> of the breast &#x0005b;see comments&#x0005d;</article-title><source>JAMA</source><year>1996</year><volume>275</volume><fpage>913</fpage><lpage>918</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'JAMA||275|913||bib6|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8598618</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fox</surname><given-names>SB</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Hollyer</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surna